You already have the HotReload package referenced. Use `dotnet test` with the `--hotreload` flag to start a watch-style session that re-runs tests whenever you save changes:

```bash
dotnet test --hotreload
```

This starts an interactive session — when you edit and save `EmailValidatorTests.cs`, tests automatically re-run without a full rebuild.

**Your failing test:** `Validate_MissingAtSign_ReturnsFalse` fails because `IsValidEmail` only checks for non-empty strings, not for an `@` sign. In your hot-reload session, fix `IsValidEmail` to something like:

```csharp
private static bool IsValidEmail(string email)
{
    return !string.IsNullOrEmpty(email) && email.Contains('@');
}
```

Save the file and the tests will automatically re-run, letting you verify the fix instantly.
